{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage","id":800575,"title":"[Hack] Alternative New Dawns - Other endings for Pilgrimage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-04T07:42:01-08:00","id":800575,"title":"[Hack] Alternative New Dawns - Other endings for Pilgrimage","content":"<i><b>Notice:</b> This is totally <b>unofficial </b>fan material and point of view. If you think, like game developers, that <b>Promethean</b> should only be about becoming human - just stop here and do not write any further. This topic is only about extending game to other &quot;endings&quot;. If you not agree with that idea - do not write, it needless and counter to the topic idea. We do not need any flame war here.</i><br /> <br /> Once again return topic of forcing Pilgrimage to be about becoming human. Inspired from two posts in latest discussion I open proper topic for this rules change ( hack ) to the base setting. As <b>Promethean</b> 2ED is just around corner I think it's proper time for it. Here are inspiration posts:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800514#post800514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could also repurpose the new dawn as a way to &quot;refine&quot;, &quot; distill&quot; or &quot;purify&quot; Azoth so that it no longer causes Disquiet, Wasteland or Torment. You will still be using the same mechanics, you will preserve the theme, and you won't have angry fans saying you're ignoring a core component of the game. :P</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800543#post800543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps the simplist solution would be to change the end-goal of the different Refinements? Each Refinement is a path towards the Great Work. Aurum reflects becoming a human by mimicking, changing to fit humanity. The path of Torment is about your base desires and living as you will. I remember someone in the past suggested that Mercury would transform you into an angel/quashmal. Etc. Its a simple and elegant solution to your question. Would that work for what you want?<br /> <br /> Tin has these Transmutations actually. I've always thought of Tin as &quot;Flux lite.&quot; The Refinement of Tin focuses on understanding and controlling your Torment, and, by extension, Wastelands and Disquiet. Torment is, by defintion, the imbalanced Flux inherant within the Promethean. So, its basically a non-evil way of studying your monstrous nature and controlling it. Meanwhile, Cobalt studies sin and indulgence and other base desires for someone who wants to go that route. Actually, both Colbalt and Tin study Disquietism, which controls the monstrous nature parts.<br /> <br /> Actually, this last one is Centimani, flat out, no change needed. They're the Promethean equivalent to the cackling necromancer overlord wannabe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Proper rules will be when the 2ED corebook will be here, but for now we could use this just system roll on the New Dawn from page 195 of 1ED corebook.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Hack - Alternative New Dawns</b></span><br /> <br /> <i>In this rules variant, Created do not look only for becoming mortal - many do, others are not interested in this. They all lives are Pilgrimage, but each one of it goes in different destination. What end story of particular Created is based on the his last Refinement he choose when making New Dawn roll. </i><br /> <br /> Basic ideas of into what Created could transform at New Dawn:<br /> <br /> <b>Aes</b> - Qashmallim, directed to the guarding other Created<br /> <b>Argentum</b> - Created that can change Pyros in to other forms of &quot;powers&quot; ( like Mana, Essence, etc. )<br /> <b>Aurum</b> - Mortal human, as per normal rules<br /> <b>Centimani</b> - Lilithim<br /> <b>Cobalus </b>- Mortal human, with Vice-Ridden or Virtuous Merit<br /> <b>Cuprum</b> - Created but without Disquiet limitations<br /> <b>Ferrum</b> - Created without limit to Attributes rising by Pyros<br /> <b>Mercurius</b> - Qashmallim, dedicated to wills of Principle<br /> <b>Phosphorum </b>- ??? ( I really do not have good idea here what to make with character )<br /> <b>Stannum</b> - Created but without Torment limitations<br /> <br /> Waiting to hear your thoughts on idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-04-2016, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T07:48:14-08:00","id":800578,"title":"","content":"They feel a bit underpowered and underwhelming to me. Like, the standard New Dawn is that you lose your major template, that's a Big. Deal.<br /> <br /> IMO that should be the golden standard that all other refinements measure up to.<br /> <br /> For example, Argentum could allow you to change your major template to another major template from the CofD, whatever one you studied the most (like the Galateid from the Argentum example could've New Dawn'd straight into a vampire).<br /> <br /> Those that want to stay the same (such as Stannum and Ferrum) should be freed from Disquiet, Torment and Wasteland altogether, not simply one.<br /> <br /> But other than that, it's a fairly good first draft, I have to say. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T08:02:36-08:00","id":800581,"title":"","content":"Silver should go to full out &quot;different supernatural.&quot; Colbalt, Copper, and Iron need something different; that's basically just repeats of Tin. Well, maybe Cobalt can stay - its effectively a variation of Tin as it is, they both share Disquietism. But Copper and Iron do need something different while Tin and cobalt get the &quot;remove drawbacks&quot; option.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest coming up with five variations, based on the standard five Refinements. The other Refinements are advanced, but still variations / combinations of the base five. I'd work from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T08:05:00-08:00","id":800584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage#post800575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Aes</b> - Qashmallim, directed to the guarding other Created<br /> <b>Argentum</b> - Created that can change Pyros in to other forms of &quot;powers&quot; ( like Mana, Essence, etc. )<br /> <b>Aurum</b> - Mortal human, as per normal rules<br /> <b>Centimani</b> - Lilithim<br /> <b>Cobalus </b>- Mortal human, with Vice-Ridden or Virtuous Merit<br /> <b>Cuprum</b> - Created but without Disquiet limitations<br /> <b>Ferrum</b> - Created without limit to Attributes rising by Pyros<br /> <b>Mercurius</b> - Qashmallim, dedicated to wills of Principle<br /> <b>Phosphorum </b>- ??? ( I really do not have good idea here what to make with character )<br /> <b>Stannum</b> - Created but without Torment limitations<br /> <br /> Waiting to hear your thoughts on idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, setting aside my prejudice to this idea, I'll have a look at this.<br /> <br /> Aes: this seems interesting if only a little weird since Quashmalims are supposed to be born and die for a singular purpose, but I suppose exceptions make the rules.<br /> Argentum: Why not humans with such a power? Or why not simply becoming a supernatural creature of your choice?<br /> Aurum: yup.<br /> Centimani: I would have rather gone with &quot;Dead&quot;, since Centimanism is explicitely not on a pilgrimage, but I could settle for &quot;Horror&quot; (as in the generic, weird monster with no neat box)<br /> Cobalus: That's just Aurum with a cherry on top, I'm not too fond of it<br /> Cuprum: Nope.<br /> Ferrum: Nope.<br /> Mercurius: basically Aes, since the will of the Principle is to help Prometheans (usually)<br /> Stannum: Nope.<br /> <br /> Ok to explain a little: Pyros (The driving component of a Promethean) is the power of <i>change</i>. That power is then either used as Flux (the destructive change, the erosion, the mutation) or Azoth (the creative change, the evolution, the creation). As such, a Promethean should never stay a Promethean as his New Dawn.<br /> <br /> Becoming a Quashmalim is a nice Idea, wether a Lilithim or an Elpidos is not important, it's a cool idea.<br /> &quot;Stay a Created but X&quot; is not an interesting idea, since it could also just be a high-level Transmutation. Having no limit on physical boosts, for example, could just be a 4-5 dots Transmutation. Torment and Disquiet Management are already Transmutations, and they're both a lot less threatening in the 2nd edition from what we've heard.<br /> I think skipping the Human step and going straight for Beast/Werewolf/Mage can be interesting (and maybe even Deviant) since they're supposed to be either non-humans or super-humans (Mage)<br /> <br /> <br /> I think that all Basic Refinements should simply lead straight to &quot;Human&quot;, while Complex Refinements could lead to something else. So, say:<br /> <br /> Aes: Athanor-Ghost (You become some sort of Athanor to help others of your kind find their place in the world)<br /> Argentum: Any other Supernatural splat, or maybe just a Spirit<br /> Cobalus: No idea<br /> Mercurius: Quashmalim (Or simply becoming a part of the Principle)<br /> Phosphorum: Not enough info.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T08:13:00-08:00","id":800588,"title":"","content":"Not at all sold on the notion. That said: nearly all of the other supernatural types have related \u201clesser templates\u201d (e.g., ghouls; wolf-blooded; Proximi; Fae-touched; etc.) \u2014 if I <i>were</i> to go with this notion, I'd probably have Argentum Redeem as a mortal with an appropriate minor template (e.g., if you've been studying werewolves and/or spirits, you end your Pilgrimage as a wolf-blooded mortal). <br /> <br /> Elsewise: note that <i>qashmallim</i> are notoriously short-lived and bound to their Missions; that's not really a \u201cstep up\u201d for a Promethean. Indeed, I'd be inclined to view a Promethean-to-<i>qashmal</i> transformation as the Promethean equivalent of dying and becoming a ghost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T11:29:13-08:00","id":800661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said: nearly all of the other supernatural types have related \u201clesser templates\u201d (e.g., ghouls; wolf-blooded; Proximi; Fae-touched; etc.) \u2014 if I <i>were</i> to go with this notion, I'd probably have Argentum Redeem as a mortal with an appropriate minor template (e.g., if you've been studying werewolves and/or spirits, you end your Pilgrimage as a wolf-blooded mortal). </div> </div> </div>That's clever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T14:13:01-08:00","id":800732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=800581#post800581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, maybe Cobalt can stay - its effectively a variation of Tin as it is, they both share Disquietism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cobalt has Deception; it's Plumbum that has the second instance of Disquietism-affinity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T20:50:34-08:00","id":800961,"title":"","content":"Next iteration of New Dawns, taking your advices in account. After list I written mine reasoning on those.<br /> <br /> <b>Aes</b> \u2013 Bronze \u2013 Qashmallim (Elpidos), directed to the guarding other Created<br /> <b>Argentum</b> \u2013 Silver \u2013 Human with Lesser Template by supernatural the practitioner was obsessed with \u2013 like Ghoul for vampires, Wolf Blooded for werewolves, Proximi for mages, Fae-Touched for fae, etc.<br /> <b>Aurum</b> \u2013 Gold - Mortal human, as per normal rules<br /> <b>Centimani</b> \u2013 Flux - Qashmallim (Lilithim) or Horror ( from <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> rulebook )<br /> <b>Cobalus</b> \u2013 Cobalt - Mortal human, with Vice-Ridden or Virtuous Merit<br /> <b>Cuprum </b>\u2013 Copper \u2013 Prefected Created<br /> <b>Ferrum</b> \u2013 Iron - Prefected Created<br /> <b>Mercurius</b> \u2013 Quicksiler \u2013 Qashmallim (Elpidos), dedicated to seeding the Principle<br /> <b>Phosphorum</b> \u2013 Phosphor - ???<br /> <b>Plumbum</b> \u2013 Lead - Prefected Created<br /> <b>Stannum</b> - Tin - Prefected Created<br /> <br /> Perfected Created means that promethean still is Created character, but he does not have Disquiet, Torment and Wasteland problems that rest of their kind still on Pilgrimage have. Idea on only one rule lifted maybe is thematic fitting, but in running will be a large problem. <br /> <br /> I went with Lesser Template idea on the Argentum, as it in reality what practitioner of Silver is \u2013 a fan of some supernatural race. Lesser Templates still can become proper \u201cmonsters\u201d, they have greater chance on this even, but it weirdly also very human to be obsessed like this on other beings. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I left Qashmallim transformations, as they are interesting and fitting to two Refinements. Also, from mine understanding of how Angels of Principle works \u2013 they <i>have</i> continued existence. They just summoned \u201cwhen they needed\u201d, so there could be hundreds of years before they return. But both Sentries and Ophidians works as \u201cultimate form\u201d as such. Also, Mercurius should be more dedicated in establishing the power of Principle in the world, where Aes are those that guard Created.<br /> <br /> With Centimani I left Lithim option, as it is interesting that your archenemy could return as power of chaos and destruction. On the other hand, becoming Horror ( like from <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> rulebook ) is logical evolution for the Freaks. As Centimani is all about contradictions and most are NPCs \u2013 they have two endings to choose from. It still will be a Storyteller choice in the end.<br /> <br /> For now we have 4 Refinements ending with becoming perfected Created, 3 about becoming Human and 3 about becoming Qashmallim. I would aim for Phosphorum with Human ending, maybe with some twist, only because we will then have nice even numbers between Refinements. Thinking about what we know about Phosphor, maybe mortal that is aging at twice rate? But this do not sound as something that players would want to aim for... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T21:23:53-08:00","id":800986,"title":"","content":"The <i>qashmallim</i> are created when their Mission begins and are disbanded when they complete the Mission or run out of juice, whichever happens first. You're free to reinterpret them, and 2e may do so; but as things stand, that's how they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T08:12:45-08:00","id":801396,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the Aes and Mercurius Prometheans believe that the Qashalim <i>they</i> become will last longer than that. Or have long-lasting and open-ending Missions. Or perhaps, just as Aurum Prometheans reconcile to the idea of dying as humans, they reconcile to the idea of their Missions one day being over and them returning to the Fire - there's no reason why wanting to be other than human must mean wanting to be immortal.<br /> <br /> Speaking of: Phosphorus isn't about transforming into anything - you accept that you existence is wrong, will always be wrong, and is going to end in destruction - but you can leave something behind, something that's better than you and better than what will destroy you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T11:04:35-08:00","id":801509,"title":"","content":"Kind of a variation, but what about (some of) the Refinements having a New Dawn of: Remove/Change some aspect of Promethean existence? You might still have Cuprum remove the Wasteland (for example), but to remove Disquiet, they need to complete the Refinement of [Whatever]. Integrates with Promethean's changing their Refinement, and makes it so each is a particular goal or step. It does extend the &quot;Pilgrimage&quot; a bit, but if you want &quot;Promethean, but none of the downsides&quot;, that seems fair.<br /> <br /> Dumb idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T17:50:31-08:00","id":801700,"title":"","content":"One idea I had for a new dawn creating a new template instead of a relatively vanilla mortal was inspired by the spirit-skinners from skinchangers- mortals who have refined the pyros within that they can transform into a quashmallim, although not fully powered ones ala the spiritskinner rules. <br /> <br /> Dark heroes from mirrors are another idea one could throw in, being &quot;humans plus.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T18:57:59-08:00","id":801726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=801396#post801396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps the Aes and Mercurius Prometheans believe that the Qashalim <i>they</i> become will last longer than that. Or have long-lasting and open-ending Missions. Or perhaps, just as Aurum Prometheans reconcile to the idea of dying as humans, they reconcile to the idea of their Missions one day being over and them returning to the Fire - there's no reason why wanting to be other than human must mean wanting to be immortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, I have less of a problem with the notion of ending up as a <i>qashmal</i> (with everything that that entails, good <i>and</i> bad) than with the notion of \u201cstill a Promethean, but without the drawbacks\u201d. <br /> <br /> Mainly, my problem is with putting \u201chuman\u201d alongside \u201cbetter than human\u201d, as opposed to \u201cother than human\u201d. The minor templates for Argentum work reasonably well as they're generally mixes of good and bad, and thus lean more toward \u201cother than\u201d rather than \u201cbetter than\u201d; but the so-called \u201cperfected Prometheans\u201d being proposed are, by definition, \u201cremove the drawbacks\u201d \u2014 the whole philosophy behind them is \u201cbetter than human\u201d. <br /> <br /> Note also that 1e had some alternatives, such as becoming a tree or an animal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-05-2016, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T05:47:48-08:00","id":836987,"title":"","content":"The closest I've come to an alternate New Dawn in the Promethean games I've played was in a crossover between mage and promethean where we (the prometheans) managed to get a cabal of mages to effectively 're-route' the effects of Disquiet and the Wasteland to an object. those effects were then centred around the object (we called them Phylacteries) and you could put them somewhere away from you so that you could stay in one place for basically as long as you like. The problem was that if the Phylactery was destroyed, the effects 'pinged' back to the promethean and immediately unleashed a Stage 4 Wasteland and high Disquiet around him. It was an enjoyable game actually. Another problem was the necessity of mages and the <i>massive </i>debt we owed them afterwards. It was fun though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T15:26:09-08:00","id":837241,"title":"","content":"A perfected Created is a human.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To not be dense, and to actively contribute, alternate &quot;New Dawns&quot; doesn't serve Promethean. They want to <i>become human</i>. It is better to <i>be human.</i> They can't escape Disquiet and the Wasteland because that happens because of their Azoth; it gives them animation, it blasts the landscape, it destroys social discourse.<br /> I do think there's a place for a set of Post-Promethean-Only Mortal Merits, and I do think there's some impetus - as some other posters mentioned - for allowing some refinements to acquire, upon successfully shucking off the horrible fate that is being one of the Created, Merits like Wolf-Blooded or Witness.<br /> I don't want that, necessarily, in the core game though; I want that in crossover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":685,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","user":"Ben Quo","date":". 02-25-2016, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T18:58:17-08:00","id":838353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=837241#post837241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A perfected Created is a human.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To not be dense, and to actively contribute, alternate &amp;quot;New Dawns&amp;quot; doesn't serve Promethean. They want to <i>become human</i>. It is better to <i>be human.</i> They can't escape Disquiet and the Wasteland because that happens because of their Azoth; it gives them animation, it blasts the landscape, it destroys social discourse.<br /> I do think there's a place for a set of Post-Promethean-Only Mortal Merits, and I do think there's some impetus - as some other posters mentioned - for allowing some refinements to acquire, upon successfully shucking off the horrible fate that is being one of the Created, Merits like Wolf-Blooded or Witness.<br /> I don't want that, necessarily, in the core game though; I want that in crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't OP say that this thread was for people who were open to the possibility of Promethean having alternate endings? &quot;All Prometheans EVER want to become human because being a Promethean sucks so much and the only way to make it better and if you don't want to do that you're PLAYING WRONG&quot; is exactly the kind of thinking we're trying to move past.<br /> <br /> I'm really glad this thread was made, though, it's definitely something that should be worked out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T01:19:43-08:00","id":838539,"title":"","content":"Stolen from other topic on similar matter as Alternative New Dawns...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/838364-transhumanist-ordo-dracul-style-refinement?p=838493#post838493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind that as long as you're trying to develop something that's supposed to coexist in a game with Prometheans-as-written, you're going to run into problems. For instance: \u201cmonsters aren't better than humanity, so much as they're <i>different</i>.\u201d This is largely managed by the fact that monsters have flaws and weaknesses as well as strengths. Now take these \u201csuper-Prometheans\u201d that are the end goal of your alternate New Dawn (BTW, don't we already have a thread for that?): they retain all of the benefits of being a Promethean and none of the drawbacks (because having all of the benefits and a better capacity to manage the drawbacks doesn't require a New Dawn, just Saturninus). This makes them better than human \u2014 which is the whole point, as I understand it.<br /> <br /> So if there's a \u201cbetter than human\u201d endgame option out there, why would any rational and informed Promethean pursue the \u201chuman\u201d endgame? As I said in the other thread, I don't have a problem with non-human \u201cNew Dawns\u201d (become <i>qashmal</i>, become animal, become plant, etc.); I only have a problem with the \u201chave your cake and eat it too\u201d Promethean-without-drawbacks and similar alternatives \u2014 and even then only if you try to put them alongside \u201cbecome human\u201d in the same setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>My answer is simple here - <b>Humanity seeking Created are looking for stoping to be Prometheans.</b> What I mean here is more better shown on exmaple. Let's say we have newly Created &quot;Adam&quot;. He was shun by the mob and humans for his inhumanity in his current state. Yet, he meets beautiful girl he falls in love with. He <b>wants</b> to be like a man from her dreams. He <b>wants</b> to stop being this &quot;thing&quot;. And his bad memories of life of Promethean push him to become human, even when there <i>could</i> be some ways to still be Created but &quot;perfected&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T02:06:40-08:00","id":838548,"title":"","content":"Adam arguably isn't being rational, given that there's an option that doesn't require him to sacrifice what he is to get what he wants. True, he's in love; so irrationality isn't exactly a surprise. But it's <i>still</i> irrational.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T04:40:07-08:00","id":838575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=838548#post838548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's <i>still</i> irrational.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it's still very <i>human</i>. Created seeking Gold want's to be &quot;real boy&quot; <i>so much</i>, he does not see very rational take on others. Which is kinda point of <b>Aurum</b>, is it not? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Argentum</b> are so supernatural fanboys that do not make conciseness choice on being Lesser Template human.<br /> <br /> <b>Cobalus</b> is <i>so </i>dedicated to Virtue or Vice he <i>cannot</i> be this uplifted Created being to be part of it. ( I assume Prometheans do not have Virtue and Vice as basic Anchors in 2ED )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T08:50:47-08:00","id":841921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=801509#post801509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of a variation, but what about (some of) the Refinements having a New Dawn of: Remove/Change some aspect of Promethean existence? You might still have Cuprum remove the Wasteland (for example), but to remove Disquiet, they need to complete the Refinement of [Whatever]. Integrates with Promethean's changing their Refinement, and makes it so each is a particular goal or step. It does extend the &quot;Pilgrimage&quot; a bit, but if you want &quot;Promethean, but none of the downsides&quot;, that seems fair.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think &quot;Promethean but with none of the downsides&quot; ought to be an option, for the reasons Dataweaver says. That <i>doesn't</i> mean you can't have a Refinement based on the idea, but what you give it instead are the Transmutations, and maybe some unique Synergies, that mitigate and manage the weaknesses. No New Dawn where it all turns to sunshine and rainbows, just an indefinite process of making better and better umbrellas.<br /> <br /> If you <i>do</i> want a New Dawn style removal of downside, then something of the power has to go too. If you don't cause a Wasteland, maybe you can't hold Pyros inside yourself any more (you'll be burned just like the you used to burn the ground) - the analogous roll to Mortality is the creation of an external Alembic to hold your Pyros. If you don't suffer Torment, you lost the ability for transhuman potential, say: those represent the same force pushing the Fire out through your body. I'm not sure what would go with Disquiet.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another option might be to make a succession of minor templates (like the ones that are starting to show up a lot in the general CoD threads) to replace human. The New Dawn makes you basically human, but with extra traits reflection the best qualities of the Refinement used to get there. Even Aurum can come with an innate empathy and high ability to connect with people. Cuprum may be a solid knowledge of yourself (which makes it easier to parse and cope with external influences). Ferrum may just be a high athleticism. Stannum may come with a forcefulness most people can't deny (anger transmuted into inspiration, basically). If you don't want to venture as far from human as a minor template, then a range of specialties and/or merits representing these traits might cover it. (Aurum, Cuprum, Ferrum, Stannum, and Aes might all work for that - with Mercurius as becoming a Qashmal, Argentum becoming a minor template related to one of the other supernaturals, and Cobalus and Plumbum becoming respectively de-Wastelanded and de-Tormented Prometheans - in this case, there'd be no de-Disquieted Promethean option, which fits maybe, given that wanting to stay Promethean <i>is</i> a rejection of humanity and claim to be better than it - and yes, I realise I haven't included Phosphorum in that list, unless it works for what's in my next paragraph).<br /> <br /> <br /> One thing that gets forgotten in the human/transhuman debate on Promethean is that this is world where souls definitively exist, humans have them and Prometheans don't, and thus it's humans rather than Prometheans who have a shot at eternity, even if they must transcend their mortal body to do it. So what would a Refinement look that regards humanity as a necessary transitional stage, but the actual goal is a good afterlife?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T09:09:55-08:00","id":841930,"title":"","content":"Well, regarding souls, remember that they are interchangeable. If a Promthean wants to have one, all they need to do is &quot;acquire&quot; one, then make it <i>theirs</i>, somehow. Maybe a Transmutation? Is this &quot;cheating&quot;? Sure! But why should that stop them?<br /> <br /> As far as Human+, what about each Refinement &quot;completed&quot; lets you get a free Merit upon becoming a shiny new human? Much like the Athanor bonuses from before. The more you master, the better your new life will be (and the closer to your former power you'll be). Up to and including simulating actual Promethean abilities (albeit at reduced power). Like Mummies who've achieved Apotheosis.<br /> <br /> Makes the New Dawn a Cost/Value consideration of: Fast, so I can stop being an unnatural monster hated by all, or delay it and enter humanity with improved knowledge and/or power?<br /> <br /> Which also invites commentary upon the Redeemed with a lot of Promethean power: were they so attached to their old abilities that they couldn't let go an appreciate humanity, or did they take their time and savor their understanding of humanity, and their powers are the result of their enlightenment?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T09:28:46-08:00","id":841939,"title":"","content":"I'm picturing a Promethean who planned ahead, left themselves a stockpile of Vitriol and Athanor-journals to give them insights into Refinements, and upon becoming mortal decides to go Alchemist and takes advantage of said stockpile. Is it cheating, and horribly harming the potential Integrity of their freshly minted, extra-purified soul? Yes, yes it is. But it gives them back whatever power they want to keep. Can't imagine said Promethean-turned-mortal-turned-Alchemist would keep anything that messes with Disquiet or Wastelands, but I imagine most other things are considered fair game.<br /> <br /> We'll have to wait and see what Alchemists have going for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T12:00:35-08:00","id":842044,"title":"","content":"I'd like to remind everyone that Prometheans do indeed have a tiny bit of a soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T12:18:47-08:00","id":842064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=842044#post842044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to remind everyone that Prometheans do indeed have a tiny bit of a soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect, then. They just need to add more &quot;mass&quot; to it. And there are plenty of raw materials lying around...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T14:14:33-08:00","id":842146,"title":"","content":"I want to point I <b>do not</b> say that there are not Created looking over the humanity - only that there should also be those that strife for other endgames.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=841921#post841921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that gets forgotten in the human/transhuman debate on Promethean is that this is world where souls definitively exist, humans have them and Prometheans don't, and thus it's humans rather than Prometheans who have a shot at eternity, even if they must transcend their mortal body to do it. So what would a Refinement look that regards humanity as a necessary transitional stage, but the actual goal is a good afterlife?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that burning Azoth is much more stable way in to immortality that becoming human.<br /> <br /> Also, as <b>ShadowKnight </b>points - <i>Maybe Created can strife for other kind of souls, not only human ones.</i> <b>Infinite Macabre</b> is still a thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-04-2016, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T17:58:55-08:00","id":842297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=841930#post841930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, regarding souls, remember that they are interchangeable. If a Promthean wants to have one, all they need to do is &quot;acquire&quot; one, then make it <i>theirs</i>, somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>The space it would occupy in a Promethean is either taken up by or directly adjacent to a concentration/aggregator of the Fire.<br /> <br /> The Fire is very directly the problem \u2014 outside the context of Redemption, the Pyros is a force which only understands lasting stability in terms of calcification and/or death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T18:35:49-08:00","id":842321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=841939#post841939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm picturing a Promethean who planned ahead, left themselves a stockpile of Vitriol and Athanor-journals to give them insights into Refinements, and upon becoming mortal decides to go Alchemist and takes advantage of said stockpile. Is it cheating, and horribly harming the potential Integrity of their freshly minted, extra-purified soul? Yes, yes it is. But it gives them back whatever power they want to keep. Can't imagine said Promethean-turned-mortal-turned-Alchemist would keep anything that messes with Disquiet or Wastelands, but I imagine most other things are considered fair game.<br /> <br /> We'll have to wait and see what Alchemists have going for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a lot like my idea that I'm thinking of calling a <a href=\"http://r.search.yahoo.com/_ylt=A0LEVyhJMtpW7YoAWT9XNyoA;_ylu=X3oDMTEyNzYzdHA4BGNvbG8DYmYxBHBvcwM2BHZ0aWQDQjE3OTNfMQRzZWMDc3I-/RV=2/RE=1457169098/RO=10/RU=https%3a%2f%2fen.wikiquote.org%2fwiki%2fDiogenes_of_Sinope/RK=0/RS=yfOQIgSAZuvWQ6kM8I5wCWBvhq4-\" target=\"_blank\">Diogenes Lantern.</a> What I'm thinking is that some Prometheans, upon seeing how fragile the human condition is, make preparations to ensure their future survival. The Lantern still attracts Pandorans, and can &quot;leak&quot; Pyros in some circumstances, causing Wasteland, Disquiet, etcetera, but the Redeemed is no longer &quot;on Fire&quot;. If the Lantern is lost, or eaten by a Pandoran, something... BAD happens to the Redeemed, not sure what yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T19:33:09-08:00","id":842350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=842321#post842321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a lot like my idea that I'm thinking of calling a <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://r.search.yahoo.com/_ylt=A0LEVyhJMtpW7YoAWT9XNyoA;_ylu=X3oDMTEyNzYzdHA 4BGNvbG8DYmYxBHBvcwM2BHZ0aWQDQjE3OTNfMQRzZWMDc3I-/RV=2/RE=1457169098/RO=10/RU=https%3a%2f%2fen.wikiquote.org%2fwiki%2fDiogene s_of_Sinope/RK=0/RS=yfOQIgSAZuvWQ6kM8I5wCWBvhq4-&amp;quot;]Diogenes</a> Lantern.[/URL] What I'm thinking is that some Prometheans, upon seeing how fragile the human condition is, make preparations to ensure their future survival. The Lantern still attracts Pandorans, and can &amp;quot;leak&amp;quot; Pyros in some circumstances, causing Wasteland, Disquiet, etcetera, but the Redeemed is no longer &amp;quot;on Fire&amp;quot;. If the Lantern is lost, or eaten by a Pandoran, something... BAD happens to the Redeemed, not sure what yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this similar or related to the &quot;Phylactery&quot; idea I've seen mentioned? I thought that one was really cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T20:43:53-08:00","id":842385,"title":"","content":"Oh, now that is an interesting idea. Sounds like a Lambda - style Athanor, one that combines two or more traits, which in this case are probably a Vitriol Fount and Refinement Mentor. The name and symbolism are just perfect for Promethean.<br /> <br /> The idea of completed Refinements granting specialized Merits taking the place of the 1e Redeemed Boons or Athanors seems like an awesome idea. Could the Redeemed gain more than one Merit per Refinement?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T00:02:03-08:00","id":842435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=842385#post842385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, now that is an interesting idea. Sounds like a Lambda - style Athanor, one that combines two or more traits, which in this case are probably a Vitriol Fount and Refinement Mentor. The name and symbolism are just perfect for Promethean.<br /> <br /> The idea of completed Refinements granting specialized Merits taking the place of the 1e Redeemed Boons or Athanors seems like an awesome idea. Could the Redeemed gain more than one Merit per Refinement?</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm suggesting is a tangible object that a Promethean creates OUTSIDE of their body, prior to the Final Azoth Roll. This object becomes a kind of &quot;Azothic Battery&quot; if you will, allowing access to at least SOME of the advantages of the Promethean condition, but shielding the world from much of the Divine Fire's destructive traits...most of the time.<br /> <br /> The bearers of such &quot;Lanterns&quot; are HUMAN, so they don't suffer the imbalanced humors of the Created, unless their humanity is compromised. (Morality 5 or less?)<br /> <br /> Using the harnessed Fire comes with a price, of course; &quot;Diogenoi&quot; can spread Disquiet and Wasteland while using any Transmutations that don't specifically negate those effects, and perhaps for a short time afterwards.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Lantern&quot; need not be a literal source of heat, light, or ignition, BTW, it could just as easily be a piece of jewelry, so long as it's something that will last a long time. Although I could see requiring that it be at least partially composed of the material corresponding to the Refinement that the Created was practicing at the time of their New Dawn.<br /> <br /> As for what happens if a &quot;Lantern&quot; is lost or destroyed, I'm not sure, maybe the &quot;Diogenean&quot; loses their memories from the Pilgrimage?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 03-05-2016, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T00:02:50-08:00","id":842436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=842350#post842350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this similar or related to the &quot;Phylactery&quot; idea I've seen mentioned? I thought that one was really cool.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, very much so.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T07:01:26-08:00","id":842537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=842146#post842146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that burning Azoth is much more stable way in to immortality that becoming human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prometheans aren't immortal, whereas humans can live on after the deaths of their physical bodies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 03-05-2016, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T08:14:10-08:00","id":842571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=842537#post842537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prometheans aren't immortal, whereas humans can live on after the deaths of their physical bodies.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what we know it's not true - there is no working afterlife in <b>CoD</b> universe. But Created do not have the corebooks we have, so the can assume even <i>less</i> than we.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T08:21:41-08:00","id":842575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=842571#post842571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what we know it's not true - there is no working afterlife in <b>CoD</b> universe. But Created do not have the corebooks we have, so the can assume even <i>less</i> than we.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no <i>confirmed</i> afterlife for the CoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T08:31:07-08:00","id":842580,"title":"","content":"\u2026assuming you don't consider the Underworld to be an afterlife.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T03:13:56-07:00","id":883621,"title":"","content":"What do you think of this layout:<ul><li>Aurum (Gold) - the Refinement of Mortality. Become mortal.<ul><li>Pinocchio achieves his dream, etc, acquires picket fence and 2.5 kids ending.</li> </ul></li> <li>Cuprum (Copper) - the Refinement of Seclusion. Disappear up their own arse - I mean, disappear from <i>mortal view</i> to become an enlightened higher being.</li> <li>Ferrum (Iron) - the Refinement of the Body. Become flat-out invulnerable. Who cares about Disquiet when nobody can hurt you?<ul><li>Alternatively: become genuinely indifferent. Ferrum's an interesting refinement philosophically.</li> </ul></li> <li>Plumbum (Lead) - the Refinement of Azoth. Become a being of pure Pyros, one with the Principle.<ul><li>Mechanically a Quasmal, in case they need to show up, but the New Dawn isn't mechanically crunchy.</li> </ul></li> <li>Stannum (Tin) - the Refinement of Torment. Explode. Seriously. Nuclear fireball, take them all with you. Call it a self-destruct.<ul><li>I like the idea thematically that any Promethean can technically switch to Stannum and blow up, killing everybody.</li> </ul></li> <li>Aes (Bronze) - the Refinement of Aid. Grant another the New Dawn (or maybe a small group), but you remain Promethean.<ul><li>Classic &quot;heroic sacrifice&quot; shtick. Sad Hulk music plays in the background as the credits roll.</li> </ul></li> <li>Argentum (Silver) - the Refinement of Other Splats. Change to another splat.<ul><li>A &quot;full&quot; supernatural template, just a mortal Psychic, whatever's appropriate for your character's focus.</li> </ul></li> <li>Cobalus (Cobalt) - Refinement of Vice. Become a mortal.<ul><li>Justification: humans are bastards.</li> </ul></li> <li>Mercurius (Quicksilver) - the Refinement of Pyros. Become the Promethean equivalent of an Archmage; call it Influence (Pyros) 7.<ul><li>Because sometimes you just want to be Superman.</li> </ul></li> <li>Phosphorum, the Refinement of Risk - you die. But happy. Maybe get one &quot;wish&quot; to resolve things.<ul><li>Gotta admit, I don't have a firm grasp on this one. They take risks, whoopee. Probably not a coincidence that this is the &quot;new&quot; splat and has the least development.</li> </ul></li> <li>Centimani (the &quot;Hundred Handed&quot;) - Refinement of Flux. Apotheosis; either become a powerful Ephemeral Entity, or some kind of maxed-stats Pandoran gribbly.<ul><li>And all the anti-transhumanists get to say &quot;told you so&quot;. The heroes blow you up in a climactic final battle ... right?</li> </ul></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 05-06-2016, 06:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T10:05:18-07:00","id":883870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=883621#post883621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think of this layout:</div> </div> </div> </div>The fundamental issue I have here is that the Pilgrimage <i>encourages</i> you to swap Refinements. I think you even get beats for it. So, associating refinements to new forms is troubling when we have people swapping around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cuprum (Copper) - the Refinement of Seclusion. Disappear up their own arse - I mean, disappear from <i>mortal view</i> to become an enlightened higher being. </div> </div> </div>Define &quot;enlightened higher being,&quot; please, because that sounds a lot like just becoming an Archmage.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ferrum (Iron) - the Refinement of the Body. Become flat-out invulnerable. Who cares about Disquiet when nobody can hurt you? </div> </div> </div> As for &quot;flat out invulnerable,&quot; I'm not a fan. Disquiet is only the tip of the iceberg when it comes to Prometheans - these are people with severe mental / emotional imbalances that cause you to lash out and hurt others. If I remember how Wastelands in 2e work, it still messes with the ability to raise simple things like gardens. Being invulnerable doesn't address any of the core problems of the Promethean condition - it just makes you appropriate Slasher material. Same with being indifferent - that basically sucks all the joy out of life, so what's the point?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plumbum (Lead) - the Refinement of Azoth. Become a being of pure Pyros, one with the Principle.<br /> Mercurius (Quicksilver) - the Refinement of Pyros. Become the Promethean equivalent of an Archmage; call it Influence (Pyros) 7. </div> </div> </div> The quashmallim (or other spirit forms) has been a popular alternative for a while now, though I'd say its more apropriate for Mercurius than Lead. Mercurius to Archmage just makes no sense to me - they have no connection to the Supernal, no enlightenment, no knowlege of Arcana, no way to use Imperial Mysteries. And becoming another supernatural really is the domain of Silver.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Stannum (Tin) - the Refinement of Torment. Explode. Seriously. Nuclear fireball, take them all with you. Call it a self-destruct. </div> </div> </div> Umm... if you want to self destruct, then don't bother with the New Dawn. Just kill yourself. This is more of a learned ability than achieving some new creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Aes (Bronze) - the Refinement of Aid. Grant another the New Dawn (or maybe a small group), but you remain Promethean. </div> </div> </div> Eh... not a fan of the idea. Still doesn't address the fundamental issues of I mention under Iron.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Argentum (Silver) - the Refinement of Other Splats. Change to another splat. </div> </div> </div> Been popular conclusion for a while.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Phosphorum, the Refinement of Risk - you die. But happy. Maybe get one &quot;wish&quot; to resolve things. </div> </div> </div> &quot;You die happy?&quot; This philosophy resolves around living life to the fullest, no matter the cost. They don't want to die, they just know that life can end at time, so they make the most of it. They are the embodiment of Carpe Diem, seizing the day for all its worth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Centimani (the &quot;Hundred Handed&quot;) - Refinement of Flux. Apotheosis; either become a powerful Ephemeral Entity, or some kind of maxed-stats Pandoran gribbly. </div> </div> </div> Centimani don't get to reach the New Dawn. They don't refine themselves, they revel in being a monstrous Promethean.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's a couple reworded &quot;You commit suicide,&quot; which is always achievable at any time, four instances of &quot;become another supernatural,&quot; and two that don't address the fundamental problems of being a Promethan and why they would want to follow the New Dawn in the first place. Honestly, I think you'd be better off with just a generic &quot;you become a qashmal or other supernatural/psychic mortal&quot; as an option in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-06-2016, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T10:14:19-07:00","id":883875,"title":"","content":"Would turning into a Hunter and offering your expertise of matters of alchemy and other types of occultism to protect humanity count?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T17:44:37-07:00","id":884185,"title":"","content":"I have to say, as much as I like the idea of Alternative Dawns, I really don't think that tying them specifically into the Refinements is the best way to go about it.<br /> <br /> Firstly, as MCN just mentioned, the idea is that Prometheans are <i>supposed</i> to swap between Refinements over the course of their Pilgrimage. You're treating them as something akin to Vampire's Covenants or Werewolf's Tribes, where the idea is that you will pick one that speaks to you and then stay with it for the rest of your life, or at least until something majorly shakes up your worldviews, and that's not how Refinements work. They're an exception to the rule, I know, but the big &quot;changing Refinements should be a rare and lifechanging event&quot; assumption isn't one made in canon.<br /> <br /> Secondly, with the stark exception of Argentum, <i>all</i> of the Refinements are based on looking at a specific <i>aspect of humanity</i>. Aes is studying human compassion, Aurum is studying human culture, Cobalus is studying human sinfulness... that's why Refinements are supposed to be something you will switch between fairly often, certainly more freely than a Changeling would change Courts or a Vampire would change Covenants. Each Refinement looks at one particular piece of the puzzle that is the human condition. Argentum, on the surface, stands apart from this; that's why it's the only Refinement to so far have a clear, unambiguously workable Alternate Dawn of &quot;Become a different sort of monster&quot;. And even then, it can be tied into the same metaphor as the others; Argentum is the Refinement of studying What Humans Are Not.<br /> <br /> Now, don't get me wrong, I like this Hack, and I'd love to see it work... but, we need to look at it from a different, because it's pretty clear by now that just &quot;Refinements up to eleven!&quot; isn't working, except in the case of Argentum. We need to find a new approach before we can make this work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T22:22:50-07:00","id":884389,"title":"","content":"Given that the game is built around a Pinnochio-style \u201cReal Boy\u201d New Dawn, this doesn't surprise me. <br /> <br /> I've said before that I have no interest in New Dawns that are unambiguously superior to ordinary humans; so \u201cperfected Prometheans\u201d who retain all of the good stuff and reject all of the bad stuff about the Promethean condition are right out. That said, there are other possibilities: a New Dawn that trades out the Promethean flaws of Torment, Disquiet, and Wasteland for some other set of flaws would be a possibility, depending on what those new flaws are and how the transition is explained. Becoming some sort of ephemeral entity would be one example of this; becoming some sort of ChroD-style Horror would be another. Becoming some sort of animal, vegetable, or mineral are other possibilities \u2014 according to the Firestorm Chronicle Anthology, it looks like Grandfather Crow actually achieved this kind of New Dawn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T22:42:44-07:00","id":899769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Define &quot;enlightened higher being,&quot; please, because that sounds a lot like just becoming an Archmage. </div> </div> </div>Archmages just gain extra super-duper powers, and really aren't anything like what I was envisioning at all. I was suggesting something like Ascension, or the version of Passing On where the ghost actually passes on - you disappear in a sparkle of light to some inaccessible higher plane.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for &quot;flat out invulnerable,&quot; I'm not a fan. Disquiet is only the tip of the iceberg when it comes to Prometheans - these are people with severe mental / emotional imbalances that cause you to lash out and hurt others. If I remember how Wastelands in 2e work, it still messes with the ability to raise simple things like gardens. Being invulnerable doesn't address any of the core problems of the Promethean condition - it just makes you appropriate Slasher material. Same with being indifferent - that basically sucks all the joy out of life, so what's the point? </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah. People quite rightly objected to the idea of &quot;you're a Promethean but without the drawbacks&quot;. This was an alternative to that idea - rather than becoming human, you remain Promethean, but the drawbacks no longer <i>bother</i> you. Magic Stoicism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mercurius to Archmage just makes no sense to me - they have no connection to the Supernal, no enlightenment, no knowlege of Arcana, no way to use Imperial Mysteries. And becoming another supernatural really is the domain of Silver. </div> </div> </div>You seem to have misread what I wrote; I said they gain Influence: Pyros 7, like a Spirit or Quashmal. Putting them on the same <i>power level</i> as an Archmage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eh... not a fan of the idea. Still doesn't address the fundamental issues of I mention under Iron. </div> </div> </div>Again, that's kind of the point. An alternate New Dawn that's the same only better in every way isn't a genuine alternative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;You die happy?&quot; This philosophy resolves around living life to the fullest, no matter the cost. They don't want to die, they just know that life can end at time, so they make the most of it. They are the embodiment of Carpe Diem, seizing the day for all its worth. </div> </div> </div>I admit, I don't have a strong a grasp on Phosphorus as I might like, but dying to achieve a wish seems firmly in their ballpark.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Centimani don't get to reach the New Dawn. They don't refine themselves, they revel in being a monstrous Promethean. </div> </div> </div>It seems absurd to me to suggest that one of the Y-splats is &quot;has no motivation or goals&quot;.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=883870#post883870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fundamental issue I have here is that the Pilgrimage <i>encourages</i> you to swap Refinements. I think you even get beats for it. So, associating refinements to new forms is troubling when we have people swapping around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, that's a good point.<br /> <br /> You could tie them to the Lineages, but that really doesn't work thematically. Maybe make it totally voluntary what your fate is?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=884389#post884389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've said before that I have no interest in New Dawns that are unambiguously superior to ordinary humans; so \u201cperfected Prometheans\u201d who retain all of the good stuff and reject all of the bad stuff about the Promethean condition are right out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>think</i> I agree with you, but it depends what you mean by &quot;unambiguously superior&quot; - what matters is whether they're an equally viable narrative goal to serve as a McGuffin, not who would win in a white-room fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 05-26-2016, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T23:01:18-07:00","id":899787,"title":"","content":"\u201cunambiguously superior\u201d means \u201cwhy would anyone who is remotely in their right mind pursue becoming human if they knew about this alternative?\u201d That is, you'd have to be ignorant, stupid, or crazy to want to become human. It's not about white-room combat, or about \u201cgame-balanced point accounting\u201d; but it <i>is</i> about there being tradeoffs \u2014 things that you would get if you became human that you have to sacrifice if you want to become X (whatever X happens to be), and vice versa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T04:08:10-07:00","id":899910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=899769#post899769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Archmages just gain extra super-duper powers, and really aren't anything like what I was envisioning at all. I was suggesting something like Ascension, or the version of Passing On where the ghost actually passes on - you disappear in a sparkle of light to some inaccessible higher plane.</div> </div> </div> </div> Umm... so, in short, you have another &quot;death&quot; option, but with a soul moving on. Meh. Chances are we're dealing with a complete loss of personality in each of these cases.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, yeah. People quite rightly objected to the idea of &quot;you're a Promethean but without the drawbacks&quot;. This was an alternative to that idea - rather than becoming human, you remain Promethean, but the drawbacks no longer <i>bother</i> you. Magic Stoicism. </div> </div> </div> You are no longer bothered by an inability to have friends or a home? That's pretty messed up, and I stand by my point. Not a fan. Plus, we can do that without a New Dawn. Its called being a Centimani. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, that's kind of the point. An alternate New Dawn that's the same only better in every way isn't a genuine alternative. </div> </div> </div> And again, this isn't a genuine alternative. The entire point of the New Dawn is to deal with these issues in some way. This is a rejection of the hope and desire for a better life that drives Prometheans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I admit, I don't have a strong a grasp on Phosphorus as I might like, but dying to achieve a wish seems firmly in their ballpark. </div> </div> </div> Its firmly outside their ballpark. They don't fear death, but they're not suicidal. There's a major difference. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems absurd to me to suggest that one of the Y-splats is &quot;has no motivation or goals&quot;. </div> </div> </div> Centimani are the rejection of the New Dawn. That's not the same as no motivation or goals. All Prometheans still have Aspirations. But the Hundred Handed definitely have said that they're happy with the way things are (even if they're lying).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T07:41:45-07:00","id":900020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=899910#post899910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Umm... so, in short, you have another &quot;death&quot; option, but with a soul moving on. Meh. Chances are we're dealing with a complete loss of personality in each of these cases.</div> </div> </div> </div>...the New Dawn already erases huge chunks of your personality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=899910#post899910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are no longer bothered by an inability to have friends or a home? That's pretty messed up, and I stand by my point. Not a fan. Plus, we can do that without a New Dawn. Its called being a Centimani.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? No, you're no longer <i>physically </i>inconvenienced by the downsides of the Promethean condition.<br /> <br /> And I'm pretty sure that's not how Centimani work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The entire point of the New Dawn is to deal with these issues in some way. This is a rejection of the hope and desire for a better life that drives Prometheans. </div> </div> </div>Literally the entire point of this thread is to provide <i>alternatives</i> to the New Dawn to fit the same narrative and mechanical role. If you're not interested in that idea, that's fine; unmodified Promethean is already perfect for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Centimani are the rejection of the New Dawn. That's not the same as no motivation or goals. All Prometheans still have Aspirations. But the Hundred Handed definitely have said that they're happy with the way things are (even if they're lying). </div> </div> </div>They're not &quot;ok with the way things are&quot;, they embrace Flux. Flux is literally change and mutation, and the Centimani seek to control and embrace it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T08:33:53-07:00","id":900061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=900020#post900020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...the New Dawn already erases huge chunks of your personality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your personality is not your concrete memory and the absurdity of claiming the endgame of Promethean is to completely negate a process that includes several forms of self-discovery should be evident.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're not &quot;ok with the way things are&quot;, they embrace Flux. Flux is literally change and mutation, and the Centimani seek to control and embrace it. </div> </div> </div>Flux is the name given to the entropic aspects of the Divine Fire, which warp and calcify and destroy and are generally distinguished from the more refined operations of the Pyros, particularly toward the goal of Elpis.<br /> <br /> The bathwater is not the baby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T11:41:50-07:00","id":900223,"title":"","content":"You can use fire to help make blade stronger, more flexible, whole, a thing to use and live with. You can also use fire to make a blade brittle, warped, and otherwise unsuable.<br /> <br /> Flux is the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T13:46:13-07:00","id":900317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=900020#post900020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...the New Dawn already erases huge chunks of your personality.</div> </div> </div> </div> Umm... That's like saying medicine for psychosis erases huge chunks of your personality. I'm going to go with a huge &quot;no&quot; with this one. New Dawn doesn't erase anything. It balances things out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What? No, you're no longer <i>physically </i>inconvenienced by the downsides of the Promethean condition. </div> </div> </div> Prometheans were never really physically inconvienced by Disquiet, Wastelands or Torment. PtC is the Resistance game; the Created are survivors first and foremost. They're built to survive all these problems. Any Promethean can head to the Wastes and jsut chill there.<br /> <br /> The real issue, however, is the fact that these things pretty much screw up any chance of having a life of some kind. Want a relationship? Want to grow a garden? Want to not have a hair trigger temper or throw yourself at the first available person when you're in need of comfort? These aren't physical dangers, they never were. They're things that affect other people, or are a psychological imbalance. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Literally the entire point of this thread is to provide <i>alternatives</i> to the New Dawn to fit the same narrative and mechanical role. </div> </div> </div> And I'm not saying to not have alternatives. I'm saying that you're missing the entire point of the game. Don't want to be human, but something else? Sure, go for it. But you need to address the real issues and flaws that Prometheans have that make their lives complete and utter shit. You are missing those issues and leaving the Promethean's life to be crappy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T03:23:37-07:00","id":900806,"title":"","content":"Alright, it was just one suggestion on a huge list. I'm sorry.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=900061#post900061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your personality is not your concrete memory and the absurdity of claiming the endgame of Promethean is to completely negate a process that includes several forms of self-discovery should be evident.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also removes your humours.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it's bad! Quite the opposite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 05-27-2016, 06:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T10:15:51-07:00","id":908414,"title":"","content":"I'm working on a mechanics/themes hack for Promethean 2e, and my concept for the New Dawn is that it's something very personal and with potentially infinite possibilities, but even rarer and more difficult than it is in canon. <br /> <br /> I'm going to have a list of possibilities, and establish that these aren't even the only ones. Examples would be: becoming human, changing lineage, becoming a different kind of supernatural creature, becoming a minor template, becoming something like a Promethean but different in some way, becoming a tree, becoming a beehive, becoming a bodiless data intelligence spread across the Internet, and so on. You'd need some connection to what you're trying to become- you can't just say &quot;I want to be a Mage&quot; if you haven't spent a lot of time studying the supernal, interacting with mages, and so on. <br /> <br /> There's also a rumor that if a Pandoran were to reach the New Dawn, they'd become a Promethean. And another that humans can reach a New Dawn too...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T13:43:28-07:00","id":945038,"title":"","content":"In reading 2E <b>Promethean</b> core I see it much more dedicated to the idea of Mortality than even 1E - and by this I start to question the reasons of Alternative New Dawns Hack. In 2E Integrity Stat is Pilgrimage and it's rising with each step till becoming human. It stops when one becomes Centimatus, for example.<br /> <br /> <b>Now if we have character in Alternative New Dawn that do not want to become human, but eyeing her as, say, Perfected Promethean?</b> Or qashmal? What to do with them and Pilgrimage stat? How to relate them? Also, what about character that 'change his mind' in last moment and when leading it's way from the 'human striving' Refinements, she steps in to inhuman one on last stage, with high Pilgrimage?<br /> <br /> <b>What about character that shifts between human and monstrous Refinements? What about Roles in Refinements?</b><br /> <br /> So many questions - I'm not so sure it's worth the tinkering with 2E rules engine aimed so hard at becoming human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T15:03:33-07:00","id":945080,"title":"","content":"<b>Firestorm Chronicle Anthology</b> included a story involving Grandfather Crow (the reanimated crow from <b>Magnum Opus</b> who wanted nothing more and nothing less than to become a normal crow) achieving his New Dawn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T15:15:41-07:00","id":945089,"title":"","content":"Well, none the less it's 'normal' to Promethean crow become normal crow. What about those aiming to be qashmal? Animal Created aiming to become as normal animal just need to follow their animal version of Pilgrimage. But when human body Created want to stay / become something inhuman, we have problem of framing Pilgrimage trait to it a bit...<br /> <br /> Also, Roles are centered on human point of view - for example are Roles like Bodyguard, Servant or Seeker for Aes really work with idea them wanting to become Qashmal? Or Roles of Examplar, Martyr and Soldier from Ferrum speak about wanting to become Perfected Promethean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-06-2016, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T15:43:05-07:00","id":945102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=945089#post945089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, none the less it's 'normal' to Promethean crow become normal crow. What about those aiming to be qashmal? Animal Created aiming to become as normal animal just need to follow their animal version of Pilgrimage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bear in mind that PtC2e doesn't provide an \u201canimal version of Pilgrimage\u201d. Grandfather Crow was very much an exception to the rules; and the fact that he was able to achieve Mortality as a crow despite the Pilgrimage <i>not</i> being set up to accommodate such a thing is a testament to the fact that nothing is truly impossible in <b>Promethean</b>. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=945089#post945089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Roles are centered on human point of view - for example are Roles like Bodyguard, Servant or Seeker for Aes really work with idea them wanting to become Qashmal? Or Roles of Examplar, Martyr and Soldier from Ferrum speak about wanting to become Perfected Promethean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ask Grandfather Crow how <i>he</i> did it. (Or not; \u201ccaw\u201d isn't a particularly informative answer.) Bear in mind though, that any alternate New Dawn <i>is</i> the exception to the rule, and that any sort of \u201cinhuman Pilgrimage\u201d is going to be in the same dilemma as an Extempore, only worse: an Extempore could, in theory, stumble across Milestones and/or find some guidance to make up for its lack of Azothic Memory; but Promethean who seeks an \u201cinhuman Pilgrimage\u201d will not find any such Milestones. I don't know how such a thing could be accomplished; but Grandfather Crow <i>is</i> a crow now, so it <i>can</i> be accomplished.<br /> <br /> (Even if I personally have zero interest in so-called \u201cPerfected Prometheans\u201d, which is a term that strikes me as every bit as much a contradiction as \u201cperfected imperfection\u201d. But I've already said my piece on that subject, earlier in this topic.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-06-2016, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T15:46:39-07:00","id":945106,"title":"","content":"I am in the Pilgramage mechanics section now, and, uh ,yeah, what Data says. The game is <i>focused </i>on humanity-of course it is-but it's easy to see where the exceptions can be achieved. It's just harder than the baseline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T16:22:35-07:00","id":945132,"title":"","content":"Been pondering more on all this and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5487\" data-vbnamecard=\"5487\">VoidDrifter</a> comment earlier in topic...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=884185#post884185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, don't get me wrong, I like this Hack, and I'd love to see it work... but, we need to look at it from a different, because it's pretty clear by now that just &quot;Refinements up to eleven!&quot; isn't working, except in the case of Argentum. We need to find a new approach before we can make this work.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Got idea how could be 'switching Refinements' thing solved</b> <b>- on choosing Alternative New Dawn we look over ALL Refinements Created pass - the one pointing most to the being kind is the end form of Promethean. </b>Each character need at <i>least</i> 4 Refinements in 2E, so trends can be extrapolate for his whole Pilgrimage. Have most human-centric Refinements? You will be human. Has most those dedicated to Pyros? You will end Qashmal. It's much less sure way of pointing 'you need to do this and this to end here', but it also makes Alternative New Dawns really possible in setting.<br /> <br /> Looking more over Roles they can be framed like they are - Roles works with archetypes dedicated to studies on Refinement. Even if shown from humanity standpoint, they connect to Ethos of it, and by this, connects to 'end-form' of particular New Dawn.<br /> <br /> EDIT: We need to better hash out possible New Dawns to have coherent rules. Here is list of possible options and Refinements I think point to them.<br /> <br /> New Dawn Ending:<ul><li>Human - Aurum, Cobalus, (Argentum), (Phosphorum )</li> <li>Quashmal - Plumbum, Aes, Mercurius</li> <li>'Perfected Created' - Cuprum, Ferrum, Stannum</li> <li>Death? - Phosphorum</li> <li>Other? - Argentum</li> </ul>Those options with '?' I'm not sure should be as possible in New Dawns. Refinements in brackets are those that would be added to the list if their New Dawn would not work.<br /> <br /> As my comment of this, I think that Death as New Dawn is least thematic for Promethean game. New Dawn is sought out, 'the Bright Day' of Created - to this being Death of Promethean could be too much.<br /> <br /> Idea of Argentum becoming Lesser Template connected to other monster is very interesting. but with mechanics of looking over 'what Refinements trends dictates', is impossible to be chosen. So probably this option will also be scrapped from list and added to Human ending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-06-2016, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T16:59:20-07:00","id":945155,"title":"","content":"That's still not addressing the fundamental problem; the existing Refinements are focused on studiying <b>aspects of humanity</b>/... so, tweaking those to become other forms of New Dawn? It's not going to work.<br /> <br /> I think the better idea here is to start from the end and work backwards. Figure out &quot;what are the alternate things a Promethean could strive to turn into?&quot; and <b>then</b> deduce backwards to find the things that could work right.<br /> <br /> Become another kind of monster, that's clearly tied into Argentum, and it works as it's a sensible end-goal. But what about trying to become an animal? Or to attain one-ness with one's inherent element(s)? What about trying to transcend this plane and find a new world - a permanent migration to the Astral, the Dreamscape, the Spirit World? What about attaining &quot;harmony&quot;, retaining some (weakened) Promethean powers &amp; general attributes but lessening the penalties, ala Mummies and their Apothesis?<br /> <br /> The New Dawn, ultimately, boils down to &quot;become something other than the incomplete creation you are&quot;. For this project to succeed, we need to stop focusing on the journey and more on the destination; once we know <b>what</b> they can become, then we can worry about the mechanics of becoming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T18:50:41-07:00","id":945216,"title":"","content":"I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> might be onto something \u2014 only it's not the Refinements that matter; it's the Roles. And every one of the thirty existing Roles is either humanocentric or neutral. So what would be needed for a successful non-human New Dawn would be new Roles oriented toward a non-human goal. Grandfather Crow probably achieved his dream by discovering and mastering crow-oriented Roles for whichever Refinements he discovered, so that when he achieved his New Dawn he was able to build his new existence out of crow-oriented Roles. Unless he passed on the knowledge of the Roles he pioneered, they're probably lost; so a hypothetical Promethean who wants to become a crow will have to rediscover them hirself. <br /> <br /> This breaks the implied rule that there are exactly three Roles per Refinement. But I have no problem with that; I'm inclined to view the lists of Roles as indicative rather than comprehensive. <br /> <br /> And I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5487\" data-vbnamecard=\"5487\">VoidDrifter</a> also has a point: before you start devising Roles that are oriented toward alternate New Dawns, it's probably a good idea to have a sense of what alternatives exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T01:24:54-07:00","id":945356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=945216#post945216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> might be onto something \u2014 only it's not the Refinements that matter; it's the Roles. And every one of the thirty existing Roles is either humanocentric or neutral. So what would be needed for a successful non-human New Dawn would be new Roles oriented toward a non-human goal.<br /> (...)<br /> And I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5487\" data-vbnamecard=\"5487\">VoidDrifter</a> also has a point: before you start devising Roles that are oriented toward alternate New Dawns, it's probably a good idea to have a sense of what alternatives exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, giving it a thought and reading New Dawn mechanics in 2E I think I may have answer...<br /> <br /> First, let's asses possible End Forms for Created. I see at least 3 of them:<ul><li>Human</li> <li>Quashmal</li> <li>'Perfected' ( Promethean )</li> </ul>You clearly are not fond of Perfected, but you can easily lose them later. Just stay with me here...<br /> <br /> Each ending is connected to one Roles category...<ul><li><b>Human</b> - Humans</li> <li><b>Quashmal </b>- Prometheans</li> <li><b>Prefected </b>- Self</li> </ul>Basiclly, depending on the profile of Roles, you divide the all 30 of them to those concepts - character with most Roles in one category ends as being of that category. <b>Plus of this solution is simple - if you do not like particular being as ending ( like you both do not like Perfected ), you can just simply made new divide list.</b><br /> <br /> If you have other other ideas for End Form, write them - maybe we will add more to the list. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As to rules for Perfected themselves - I will go with number of Refinments decidieng easeing Promethean Drawbacks, just like original New Dawns mechnics give you better 'start' in human life. For now I'm thinking on one benefit per 3 Refinments future Perfected got on his Pilgrimage. Possible effects for them are:<ul><li>Stopping creating Disquiet</li> <li>Stopping creating Wasteland</li> <li>Stopping going into Torment</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T04:44:52-07:00","id":945402,"title":"","content":"I am not going to provide any sort of constructive criticism on so-called \u201cPerfected Prometheans\u201d. It's not just (or even primarily) a matter of disliking them; it's that they're poorly conceived, and smack of the worst kind of power-gaming: that which is executed with a total lack of imagination. They're like taking werewolves and stripping then if their death-rage and vulnerability to silver. Not just providing ways to downplay or overcome them, but flat-out eliminating them.<br /> <br /> Your list of \u201cpossible end forms\u201d excludes the one alternative to human that has been confirmed by canon: namely, animals. <b>Strange Alchemies</b> also hints at a Promethean who became a tree. I don't mind <i>qashmallim</i> being on the list, because their lives are short and tightly focused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T06:22:42-07:00","id":945426,"title":"","content":"Well, it's not Power Gaming if it is end of story - you will only get Perfected as those rare NPC ancient masters of Created that wanted to be their own kind rather than forced to be human by Principle. ( See an Extempore write-up for ideas on those. )<br /> <br /> Animals and trees do not sounds to me as something you can strife for in more individual cases - those that you started as 'body' from this kind. Even then, they clearly could be in the Self category.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-07-2016, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T08:40:51-07:00","id":945477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=945426#post945426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it's not Power Gaming if it is end of story - you will only get Perfected as those rare NPC ancient masters of Created that wanted to be their own kind rather than forced to be human by Principle. ( See an Extempore write-up for ideas on those. )</div> </div> </div> </div>Extempore have exactly the same drive to become human as every other Promethean. What they lack is the <i>guidance</i> that shows other Prometheans how to do it. <br /> <br /> Also: Disquiet, Wasteland, and Torment aren't the Principle trying to push a Promethean to become human; they're the nature of Pyros asserting itself. Pyros is harmful to the environment; that's why Wastelands form. Pyros is harmful to the human psyche; that's why people experience Disquiet. And Pyros is volatile and unstable; that's why Prometheans experience Torment. It's the <i>nature of what a Promethean is</i>, not an outside force punishing the Promethean for not doing its will \u2014 that's what <i>Lilithim</i> are all about. A Promethean that doesn't deal with Wasteland, Disquiet, or Torment is like a fire that doesn't burn. <br /> <br /> You want a Promethean whose goal is to settle down and live comfortably as a Promethean? Go Centimani, or settle into a Role. Sure, a <i>qashmal</i> will eventually come knocking to try to rouse you from the rut you're in; but only <i>one</i> will come, <i>ever</i>: <i>qashmallim</i> do not repeat failed Missions. So if you can overcome that one <i>qashmal</i>, you're free of the Principle's interference. Also, consider setting up a Hovel, so that you can live comfortably in your Safe Place without worrying about creating a Wasteland; and if you stick with a Role that you've mastered, you don't have to worry about Disquiet either. That leaves only Torment, which isn't going to go away so long as you have Azoth burning inside of you. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=945426#post945426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Animals and trees do not sounds to me as something you can strife for in more individual cases - those that you started as 'body' from this kind. Even then, they clearly could be in the Self category.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. I could see a humanoid Promethean who encounters and befriends a dog growing to admire his furry companion, and eventually deciding he wants to become a dog, too. Yes, Prometheans with \u201cbecome an animal\u201d as a final goal are likely to be rare; but Prometheans with a final goal other than \u201cbecome human\u201d are rare to begin with. <br /> <br /> 2. I don't know what category they'd be in; I could see a case for an animalistic Iron Role for a Promethean seeking to become, say, a housecat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T09:29:39-07:00","id":945495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=945477#post945477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Extempore have exactly the same drive to become human as every other Promethean. What they lack is the <i>guidance</i> that shows other Prometheans how to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was meaning this idea in Extempore write-up:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PtC 2E, p.39</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Extempore are also likely to become immortals, lost forever in the sea of humanity. Without any model for how to complete the Great Work and achieve humanity, Extempore can lose their way; if any of the Created are going to be blessed (or cursed) with a spark of Pyros that never dies, it is going to be one of the Matchless, who so often bend the rules about what it means to be a Promethean. In this way, Extempore can sometimes become the keepers of Promethean history. They may remain nomadic, or they might find someplace in the wilderness where their Wastelands won\u2019t harm anyone, waiting for other Created to come looking for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It basic concept idea for Perfected NPCs. You can not like them, but I think it's viable character that would not want to be human at New Dawn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=945477#post945477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also: Disquiet, Wasteland, and Torment aren't the Principle trying to push a Promethean to become human; they're the nature of Pyros asserting itself. Pyros is harmful to the environment; that's why Wastelands form. Pyros is harmful to the human psyche; that's why people experience Disquiet. And Pyros is volatile and unstable; that's why Prometheans experience Torment. It's the <i>nature of what a Promethean is</i>, not an outside force punishing the Promethean for not doing its will \u2014 that's what <i>Lilithim</i> are all about. A Promethean that doesn't deal with Wasteland, Disquiet, or Torment is like a fire that doesn't burn.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right that they are part of Divine Fire - but also we have Transmutations like <i>Disquietism</i>, that mean the Created <b>can</b> control those powers. Or <i>Sanctuary</i> Athanor that calms her Disquite and Torment. Perfected New Dawn ending would remake character like after those permanent Transmutation and Athanor - maybe not totally forsaking those problems, but facilitate them to be delt with. I think it's more than probable in terms of game world, as character <i>without hack </i>have tools for things like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=945477#post945477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You want a Promethean whose goal is to settle down and live comfortably as a Promethean? Go Centimani, or settle into a Role.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great advice - become serial killer or be stuck in point of your life forever. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> No, I do not think it's 'good ending' for character after whole Pilgrimage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=945477#post945477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, consider setting up a Hovel, so that you can live comfortably in your Safe Place without worrying about creating a Wasteland; and if you stick with a Role that you've mastered, you don't have to worry about Disquiet either. That leaves only Torment, which isn't going to go away so long as you have Azoth burning inside of you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for those advises as player character - I will use them if I will be playing not running game anywhere, <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Still, it's temporary solution, not 'good ending' for character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=945477#post945477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. I could see a humanoid Promethean who encounters and befriends a dog growing to admire his furry companion, and eventually deciding he wants to become a dog, too. Yes, Prometheans with \u201cbecome an animal\u201d as a final goal are likely to be rare; but Prometheans with a final goal other than \u201cbecome human\u201d are rare to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just go and change then Perfected ending into animal one - they will work for it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=945477#post945477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. I don't know what category they'd be in; I could see a case for an animalistic Iron Role for a Promethean seeking to become, say, a housecat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do not know what you mean here, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-07-2016, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T10:59:55-07:00","id":945551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=945495#post945495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was meaning this idea in Extempore write-up:<br /> <br /> It basic concept idea for Perfected NPCs. You can not like them, but I think it's viable character that would not want to be human at New Dawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>So basically, you're talking about an immortal Promethean. Sure, that's fine; it's basically a riff off of the sample Extempore from <b>Magnum Opus</b>, who had a Bestowment that let him Return from death any number of times with no ill effect. That's not what I'd call \u201cPerfected\u201d, though. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=945495#post945495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are right that they are part of Divine Fire - but also we have Transmutations like <i>Disquietism</i>, that mean the Created <b>can</b> control those powers. Or <i>Sanctuary</i> Athanor that calms her Disquite and Torment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said that these things can't be <i>controlled</i>; only that they can't be <i>eliminated</i>. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=945495#post945495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perfected New Dawn ending would remake character like after those permanent Transmutation and Athanor - maybe not totally forsaking those problems, but facilitate them to be delt with.</div> </div> </div> </div>As you point out, there are already mechanisms in the game for coping with Wasteland, Disquiet, and Torment; and they can be quite effective as is. I don't see how they could be \u201cupgraded\u201d without taking them into the realm of negating the trouble in question entirely. And if they <i>do</i> eliminate it, you're dealing with a situation where the proposed <i>alternative</i> to the New Dawn is <i>superior</i> to the New Dawn. Which completely undermines the themes of the game. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=945495#post945495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great advice - become serial killer or be stuck in point of your life forever. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> No, I do not think it's 'good ending' for character after whole Pilgrimage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two points: Centimani aren't serial killers; they're Prometheans who have abandoned the Pilgrimage. And living in a rut isn't the <i>ideal</i> ending, no; but if you consider \u201cbecoming human\u201d to be a horrendous option, it's a decent alternative. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=945495#post945495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for those advises as player character - I will use them if I will be playing not running game anywhere, <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Still, it's temporary solution, not 'good ending' for character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course it isn't. The \u201cgood ending\u201d is to become human. <br /> <br /> More generally, you seem to be aiming for a \u201cfree lunch\u201d, where you get to keep all of the benefits of the Divine Fire while suffering none of the drawbacks. That's what I meant by the \u201cpower gaming\u201d remark earlier. Why do the various \u201ctrouble mitigator\u201d suggestions not work? Because they have their own drawbacks,and thus aren't \u201cgood endings\u201d. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=945495#post945495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do not know what you mean here, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're insisting that an animal-oriented Role would fall under Self; I'm suggesting that it could fall under a number of Refinements, and am using Body as an example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T14:29:50-07:00","id":945665,"title":"","content":"Not going to get involved with you two chewing bits off of each other, but personally, in my games, my &quot;perfected&quot; Promethean would be a &quot;Harmonious&quot; one - like a Mummy who has achieved Apothesis, they have reduced or removed their inherent drawbacks, but they've <b>also</b> reduced most of their supernatural powers. That's the price one pays for carefully banking and damping the Divine Fire; it no longer burns uncontrollably, but it cannot burn as intensely, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T18:39:42-07:00","id":945796,"title":"","content":"I think my ideal approach would be the hack the rules so that Prometheans are closer to vampires or werewolves: they have their kewl powerz but major drawbacks, but drawbacks that are manageable enough that they can maintain themselves indefinitely (yet dangerous and volatile enough that they're genuinely risky and mitigating with them and working around them provides plot hooks). <br /> <br /> I'd also have the New Dawn be much closer to Golconda or DtD's version of Hell: something elusive and widely rumored, that's highly personal and could be any number of things, and are primarily narrative rather than mechanical. <br /> <br /> Something like the &quot;Harmonious&quot; idea above could be a New Dawn option, as would becoming human or becoming another supernatural creature.<br /> <br /> The fact that Pilgrimage is the &quot;morality stat&quot; confirms that I'm going to have to do a major stat of this, because that clearly needs a ton of work. I was hoping I wouldn't have much to do, but it's looking like my eventual result is going to be pretty long. Maybe not necessarily as long as my full remake of Mage (I don't think I'll have to completely rewrite the mechanics for this one), but long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 08-07-2016, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T18:45:54-07:00","id":945798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=899787#post899787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cunambiguously superior\u201d means \u201cwhy would anyone who is remotely in their right mind pursue becoming human if they knew about this alternative?\u201d That is, you'd have to be ignorant, stupid, or crazy to want to become human. It's not about white-room combat, or about \u201cgame-balanced point accounting\u201d; but it <i>is</i> about there being tradeoffs \u2014 things that you would get if you became human that you have to sacrifice if you want to become X (whatever X happens to be), and vice versa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pfffft, if you want to play an enlightened supernatural being so obviously superior to humanity that no one would choose to be anything else, you have Mage for that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T19:44:34-07:00","id":945842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=945477#post945477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> like a fire that doesn't burn.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I am so SICK of the &quot;you're on fire&quot; argument. Almost nothing about how Pyros behaves really matches up with fire, anyway! A Promethean can ...&quot;live&quot; for a hundred years or more, what kind of fire does that? And <a href=\"http://comicvine.gamespot.com/jim-hammond/4005-12605/\" target=\"_blank\">here's</a> an example of an artificial human who's been around for about 75 years,. Go ahead, talk to him about being on fire.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T19:52:30-07:00","id":945850,"title":"","content":"Chill, please. I wasn't invoking the\u201cyou're on fire\u201d argument (i see nothing wrong with it; but that's irrelevant to the current discussion). I was pointing out a logical impossibility: something that lacks one of its defining traits. Fire, by definition, burns; so saying that you want fire that doesn't burn is ridiculous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T19:59:40-07:00","id":945855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=945850#post945850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chill, please. I wasn't invoking the\u201cyou're on fire\u201d argument (i see nothing wrong with it; but that's irrelevant to the current discussion). I was pointing out a logical impossibility: something that lacks one of its defining traits. Fire, by definition, burns; so saying that you want fire that doesn't burn is ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, you could easily make the point that when you're an undead being with amazing powers who has the ability to become human by what's been described as a literal miracle, &quot;fire that doesn't burn&quot; is well within the scope of things you can imagine existing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T20:24:04-07:00","id":945875,"title":"","content":"I just had a breakthrough: Following a similar logic to the &quot;harmonious&quot; idea, how about a Pilgrimage 10 Promethean can enter a &quot;balanced&quot; state, in which their Humors are, well, balanced:<br /> <br /> In this state, Transmutations are limited to 3 dots, but Disquiet and Wasteland only kick in when a Pilgrimage/Integrity roll, which also results in a full-on Torment freakout. A Promethean can stay in this state indefinitely, and can lead relatively normal lives, so long as they don't flip out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWs