follow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, you could easily make the point that when you're an undead being with amazing powers who has the ability to become human by what's been described as a literal miracle, &quot;fire that doesn't burn&quot; is well within the scope of things you can imagine existing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent point! And everlasting flames are a reoccurring feature in most mythology/religions.<br /> <br /> Regarding the idea of &quot;Perfected Prometheans&quot;, how about the following;<br /> <br /> Disquiet only occurs when Disfigurements are showing.<br /> Wastelands only happen during Torment.<br /> Perfected Prometheans are kinda the opposite of Vampires; they become sluggish after sundown, and maybe lose access to Transmutations, and have trouble regaining Pyros.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T21:53:25-07:00","id":945947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=945886#post945886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2e, Transmutations don't have dot ratings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not know that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T22:12:55-07:00","id":945953,"title":"","content":"Yeah; in 2e, each Transmutation has four Alembics, each of which has a Persistent power and three Distillations (which have escalating costs: the first always costs 1 Pyros, the second always costs 2 Pyros, and the third always costs 3 Pyros). The point is that when you have access to a particular Alembic, you have access to all of its powers as long as you have enough Pyros on hand to fuel them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T00:21:57-07:00","id":945997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=945842#post945842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Promethean can ...&quot;live&quot; for a hundred years or more, what kind of fire does that?</div> </div> </div> </div>A coal seam fire can potentially burn for thousands of years, for what it's worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":627,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/627-mr-innes","user":"Mr Innes","date":". 08-08-2016, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/627-mr-innes","name":"Mr Innes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T00:43:13-07:00","id":946001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=945855#post945855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, you could easily make the point that when you're an undead being with amazing powers who has the ability to become human by what's been described as a literal miracle, &quot;fire that doesn't burn&quot; is well within the scope of things you can imagine existing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It''s exactly my point! If half-alive corpses can become proper humans ( or even 'humans with powers', see mechanics in 2E of New Dawn with 10 Refinements passed ), 'angels', animals or trees - Why cannot they become 'Perfected' or 'cooled' fire? This all is miracle, one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T00:51:34-07:00","id":946003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=945944#post945944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the idea of &quot;Perfected Prometheans&quot;, how about the following;<br /> <br /> Disquiet only occurs when Disfigurements are showing.<br /> Wastelands only happen during Torment.<br /> Perfected Prometheans are kinda the opposite of Vampires; they become sluggish after sundown, and maybe lose access to Transmutations, and have trouble regaining Pyros.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting... I would compare them to the Sanctuary Athanor rules, as was thinking before about using those. Basically in my take, Created when becoming Perfected change <i>himself</i> into Sanctuary Athanor on New Dawn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PtC 2E, p.181</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Sanctuary</b><br /> When around a Sanctuary Athanor, the Promethean\u2019s dice pool for causing Disquiet is reduced to a chance die; rolls to resist Torment do not suffer the Promethean\u2019s Azoth as a penalty. It also prevents Pandorans from discovering anyone near. A Sanctuary\u2019s effects extend out two yards per dot of the creator\u2019s Pilgrimage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, 'Perfected' would <i>only</i> work on himself, he will not have radius of yards around him effect.<br /> <br /> Well this and immortality, probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-08-2016, 03:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T01:03:56-07:00","id":946009,"title":"","content":"See, I'm sticking with &quot;all power has a cost&quot; and all that, so I would want every possible option to take that into consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T20:29:15-07:00","id":947452,"title":"","content":"Some of my own thoughts on Alternative New Dawns.<br /> ------<br /> I am oddly enamoured with the idea of an Argentum Promethean becoming infatuated with the Uratha, then striving toward becoming one of them instead of Human. Hunting alongside them with the Refinement of Aurum and using Ferrum to shape their body to match. It would be an interesting approach to a Crossover game, or even a cool character for Promethean alone.<br /> There are other Supernaturals that they could aspire to, but would likely involve becoming Human first. Then there's the Unchained, which would be a really weird thing for a Promethean to want to become.<br /> <br /> If I were to run the 'Perfected Promethean' thing, I would take one of two approaches.<br /> The Centimani approach would essentially be embracing monstrosity. They would no longer suffer Torment, but their Wastelands and Disquiet are even worse. They have come to accept their monstrosity and gained all the more power for it; the world hates them all the more, but they can -endure- that hate. They've forever lost the New Dawn, but a Centimani who makes such a choice is unlikely to care.<br /> The 'Balanced' approach isn't really an ending to the Pilgrimage, it's more like stalling it indefinitely. A Balanced Promethean manages to make the Azoth 'immortal' and put an end to the Wasteland, but may not rise their Azoth beyond one (or possibly two) dots. They have accepted Isolation so they still experience Disquiet, but their Torment (while still present) is greatly lessened. The New Dawn might still call to them, but they must work even harder if they want to once again walk their Pilgrimage. This is so it feels less like Prometheans are pushed into the New Dawn and more like they can choose it for themselves.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of a Promethean pursuing something new. If a Promethean can become a Human, even an animal or a Supernatural creature-... Could they become something else? They don't necessarily want to be more than Human, nor do they necessarily want to remain a Promethean; but they believe that within them lies the genesis of something new and different. There is no word for what they want to be. If they could achieve it they would be a trailblazer among Prometheans, like the Seer before them.<br /> Truth be told, I don't even necessarily like the idea of this type of Promethean achieving their own vision of the New Dawn. But I like the idea of them pursuing it. Maybe it's impossible to achieve, maybe it can't be done; but to them, it's worth pursuing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T04:55:25-07:00","id":952432,"title":"","content":"Fleshed out the idea of the Centimani embrace of monstrosity a bit more. It's mostly a villainous thing, but I could see it being a villain protagonist thing. Fundamentally, its a rejection of the Pilgrimage and what it stands for, which seems oddly appropriate.<br /> I mostly just wanted to give something to Centimani that wasn't a dead end. Though it will take a whole lot more work than this, think of it as a framework.<br /> ------<br /> <b>Icchantika</b><br /> It is possible for a Centimanus to achieve their own monstrous apotheosis, if they are willing to seek it out. The Promethean condition is fundamentally one of change, but that change may be directed in the other direction than the Humanity that most Prometheans seek. Though there are no confirmed cases of a successful transformation, there are whispers among Pilgrims and Centimani alike of these terrifying creatures; they are sometimes called Icchantika, for they have turned their backs on the salvation offered by the New Dawn.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> There is a procedure that a Centimanus may learn, which allows them to begin their Metamorphosis into an Icchantika.<br /> Firstly, their Azoth must be strong enough to begin, then they must create a particular 'Athanor of Defilement'.<br /> Secondly, their Pilgrimage must be at its lowest possible point, then they must expend a certain quantity of Vitriol while touching the aforementioned Athanor.<br /> Finally, they must summon a terrible Firestorm upon their current location and receive a 'Flux Vision' which hints at the first steps of their new journey.<br /> <br /> A Centimanus who has begun the process undergoes several changes.<br /> They lose their Elpis and replace it with a Flux, which defines the nature of the monstrosity they seek to become. They replace their Pilgrimage with Antithesis, which tracks their progress toward their Metamorphosis; if Antithesis falls below one, they may decide to return to their Pilgrimage or continue their current path. They also resume their production of Vitriol, which fuels their journey just as surely as any Pilgrim.<br /> An aspiring Icchantika must seek the Blasphemies - Roles which twist and mock each of the Refinements - if they ever want to complete their transformation. They must complete at least five Blasphemies, then bring their Antithesis and Azoth up to ten, before they can attempt the Metamorphosis.<br /> <br /> An Icchantika is a unique monstrosity, entirely divorced from their previously Humanoid form. They possess an incredible amount of power and must be destroyed utterly if there is to be any hope of them staying dead. They possess a fully rational mind, although not necessarily one that can be understood easily by Humans. They spread Disquiet and Wastelands wherever they go. Icchantika can breed with one another, but the offspring are born considerably weaker.<br /> If any Icchantika currently exist in the world, or indeed have ever existed, they have hid themselves incredibly well. Perhaps there are one or two in the places where few Humans dwell, such as under the Sea or the wastes of Antarctica.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> ------<br /> I might write some stuff regarding the other possibilities I discussed above, among others. If I actually get around to/am able to write rules for it all I will start my own thread, but that isn't necessarily likely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":203,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","user":"Kleptomania","date":". 08-17-2016, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T06:37:06-07:00","id":952469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=945953#post945953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah; in 2e, each Transmutation has four Alembics, each of which has a Persistent power and three Distillations (which have escalating costs: the first always costs 1 Pyros, the second always costs 2 Pyros, and the third always costs 3 Pyros). The point is that when you have access to a particular Alembic, you have access to all of its powers as long as you have enough Pyros on hand to fuel them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I guess the equivalent of limited dots would be only the persistent effect. Your Azoth can't flare any more - on the plus side, this means it won't flare up into Disquiet, Torment, or Wasteland - on the minus side, you can no longer power Distillations, and can no longer gain or calcify new Transmutations or even new Alembics of existing ones (after all, the phrase being used is &quot;perfected Promethean,&quot; and if you're perfected, by definition there's no room for improvement).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T07:13:42-07:00","id":952491,"title":"","content":"If you've completed the Pilgrimage, you're not going to be on any Refinements or studying any Roles; so yes, the only Alembics you'd have would be the ones you've previously calcified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T10:10:51-07:00","id":952588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=952491#post952491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you've completed the Pilgrimage, you're not going to be on any Refinements or studying any Roles; so yes, the only Alembics you'd have would be the ones you've previously calcified.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's Refinement Furnaces to consider, too, mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T03:31:12-07:00","id":953740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=952588#post952588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's Refinement Furnaces to consider, too, mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have the book yet; would you mind elaborating on those?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T06:33:54-07:00","id":953794,"title":"","content":"They're cheaper than calcifying an Alembic (one Vitriol versus two) and are either a mark of some kind on the Promethean's body or an object they can carry around. So long as they are in possession of the Refinement Furnace they gain all the benefits of being in the Refinement without actually still being in the Refinement.<br /> <br /> This is a very loose summary- I don't have my book on me right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T08:26:58-07:00","id":953855,"title":"","content":"Note that you also only get to make a Refinement Furnace once you've mastered the Refinement; so \u201call the benefits\u201d means full access to every Alembic of both of the Refinement's Transmutations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T09:28:44-07:00","id":953883,"title":"","content":"Cheers, with enough extra characters to let me post it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T09:29:57-07:00","id":955644,"title":"","content":"So, I've been doing some thinking about the New Dawn and, currently, these are the &quot;Paths&quot; I can see a Promethean walking towards. The base assumption here is that the Promethean state is inherently unstable; they're raw, unformed, living potential. The World doesn't care what a Promethean is, it cares that it <b>becomes</b> something else, and thus every Promethean is on a journey - it's what the destination is that really differentiates them.<br /> <br /> <u>The Path of the Mortal</u><br /> This is the default Pilgrimage, the journey to become human. Humans make up the dominant lifeform on the planet, they have the most advanced and ubiquitous society, they are the closest things to the not-a-thing that is a Promethean's inherent state. Naturally, many Prometheans seek to become a human, because that's the easiest way to belong.<br /> <br /> <u>The Path of the Elemental</u><br /> These Prometheans take the &quot;become a part of the world&quot; aspect of their ideology all too literally. Most appealing to Unfleshed and Extempores, the path of the Elemental seeks to attain a physical and spiritual unity with the land itself, seeking to dampen their Azoth until it no longer scorches the land, but blends harmoniously with its own natural energies. For some of these Prometheans, the New Dawn is an act of physical and spiritual dissolution; when the Pyros fades, all that is left is a singular terrain feature, or a patch of unnaturally healthy and vital land. For others, it is a transcendence; their flesh becomes a tree, a rock, a grove, a spring, but their soul lives on as a strong and vibrant new elemental spirit.<br /> <br /> <u>The Path of the Beast</u><br /> Some Prometheans look at humans and see only things to be disgusted at. Animals are much purer; they don't lie, they don't cheat, they don't steal, they just do what nature intends for them. No guilt, no remorse, no despair. These Prometheans seek to find a place for themselves amongst the animals, eventually shedding the human form and complications they so loathe to attain that pure, blissful, instinct-driven place in nature.<br /> <br /> <u>The Path of the Monster</u><br /> When Prometheans become aware of the creatures that live in the dark places of the world, and see humanity's role as prey, they sometimes choose to follow this Pilgrimage, seeking to attain perfection as a predator. Usually following the Refinements of Argentum and Cobalus to their true mastery, and perhaps Centimanus if one discards its &quot;stagnant&quot; motif for 1e's version, a Promethean who attains this &quot;New Dusk&quot; may become a member of an existing monstrous race, or it may become some new form of horror. Whatever it becomes, it is happy, for it has found its own place in the dark places of the world.<br /> <br /> <u>The Path of the Quenched</u><br /> Hardest of all the paths to walk, the Path of the Quenched opens itself to Prometheans who ask &quot;why am I wrong? Why must I give up all that I am in order to complete myself?&quot; Though they must transcend their initial, imperfect state, they do so under the ideology that metal which has been cast must still be tempered and quenched, rather than melted down to something else. The New Dawn these pilgrims achieve creates something akin to a Mummy who has attained Apothesis; they lack the raw mystical might of their initial self, but they also no longer suffer the extremes of Pyric burn, either.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, these are the New Dawns I can see a Promethean potentially pursuing. What other ones can <b>you</b> see?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:03:29-07:00","id":955656,"title":"","content":"Well, in The Lightning Chronicle, I'm moving away from Pilgrimages having a defined ending or even defined paths. For one thing, attaining the New Dawn is very rare, rare enough that ST's can rule that it isn't even possible. In TLC, a Pilgrimage is a deeply personal experience, and the ending is purely defined by the Promethean. It's such a rare and personal thing that defined &quot;paths&quot; haven't really emerged. <br /> <br /> If I were going to keep the Pilgrimage was a more central element, I might go with VoidDrifter's excellent ideas, but as it is I don't want to give it too much weight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:36:26-07:00","id":955680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=955644#post955644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've been doing some thinking about the New Dawn and, currently, these are the &quot;Paths&quot; I can see a Promethean walking towards. The base assumption here is that the Promethean state is inherently unstable; they're raw, unformed, living potential. The World doesn't care what a Promethean is, it cares that it <b>becomes</b> something else, and thus every Promethean is on a journey - it's what the destination is that really differentiates them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This Shard, I can get behind. With one or two exceptions, I could see each of these Paths keying off of one or two new Roles reflecting the Paths destination. In order for that destination to be a result of the New Dawn, one such Role must be part of the Pilgrimage; and as many other Roles as possible must be completed in a way that emphasizes that goal. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=955644#post955644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>The Path of the Mortal</u><br /> This is the default Pilgrimage, the journey to become human. Humans make up the dominant lifeform on the planet, they have the most advanced and ubiquitous society, they are the closest things to the not-a-thing that is a Promethean's inherent state. Naturally, many Prometheans seek to become a human, because that's the easiest way to belong.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also the one that doesn't require any modifications to the basic Pilgrimage. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=955644#post955644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>The Path of the Elemental</u><br /> These Prometheans take the \u201cbecome a part of the world\u201d aspect of their ideology all too literally. Most appealing to Unfleshed and Extempores, the path of the Elemental seeks to attain a physical and spiritual unity with the land itself, seeking to dampen their Azoth until it no longer scorches the land, but blends harmoniously with its own natural energies. For some of these Prometheans, the New Dawn is an act of physical and spiritual dissolution; when the Pyros fades, all that is left is a singular terrain feature, or a patch of unnaturally healthy and vital land. For others, it is a transcendence; their flesh becomes a tree, a rock, a grove, a spring, but their soul lives on as a strong and vibrant new elemental spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice! Now, what Roles do you see aligning with this Path?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=955644#post955644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>The Path of the Beast</u><br /> Some Prometheans look at humans and see only things to be disgusted at. Animals are much purer; they don't lie, they don't cheat, they don't steal, they just do what nature intends for them. No guilt, no remorse, no despair. These Prometheans seek to find a place for themselves amongst the animals, eventually shedding the human form and complications they so loathe to attain that pure, blissful, instinct-driven place in nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside the fact that most \u201chumans are the only animals who\u2026\u201d saying are myths, this Path is about as close to canonical as any of the non-human Paths has managed to be, Great-Grandfather Crow and all. As with the previous one, I'd like to know what Roles to pursue in order to achieve this end. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=955644#post955644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>The Path of the Monster</u><br /> When Prometheans become aware of the creatures that live in the dark places of the world, and see humanity's role as prey, they sometimes choose to follow this Pilgrimage, seeking to attain perfection as a predator. Usually following the Refinements of Argentum and Cobalus to their true mastery, and perhaps Centimanus if one discards its \u201cstagnant\u201d motif for 1e's version, a Promethean who attains this \u201cNew Dusk\u201d may become a member of an existing monstrous race, or it may become some new form of horror. Whatever it becomes, it is happy, for it has found its own place in the dark places of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, this one's easy: an Argentum Role that centers around <i>being</i> the other, rather than <i>interacting with</i> the other. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=955644#post955644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>The Path of the Quenched</u><br /> Hardest of all the paths to walk, the Path of the Quenched opens itself to Prometheans who ask &quot;why am I wrong? Why must I give up all that I am in order to complete myself?&quot; Though they must transcend their initial, imperfect state, they do so under the ideology that metal which has been cast must still be tempered and quenched, rather than melted down to something else. The New Dawn these pilgrims achieve creates something akin to a Mummy who has attained Apothesis; they lack the raw mystical might of their initial self, but they also no longer suffer the extremes of Pyric burn, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not properly a Path, IMHO, as you never become something else. Rather, it's the result of gathering the necessary tools to mitigate the downsides of the Saturnine Night and then stepping off the Path indefinitely. Remember, the Promethean's existence is <i>inherently</i> unstable; no matter how much you tone it down, that instability will remain for as long as you remain a Promethean. Still, tools such as Going To The Wastes can be used to reduce your Azothic Radiance and to dampen Torment, while completing multiple Roles can ironically give you more flexibility when camping on a Role to avoid Disquiet. And since time spent in a Hovel doesn't count toward festering a Wasteland, setting up one of those gives you a way to keep the Wasteland effect in check without being forced to move away. Do all these things, and you can lead a reasonably comfortable life as a Promethean. <br /> <br /> But you're <i>still</i> a Promethean, fully capable of taking up the Pilgrimage once again whenever you choose to. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800575-hack-alternative-new-dawns-other-endings-for-pilgrimage?p=955644#post955644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, these are the New Dawns I can see a Promethean potentially pursuing. What other ones can <b>you</b> see?</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking \u201cGoing to the Wastes\u201d to the extreme, and releasing <i>all</i> of your Azoth, truly quenching the flame and ending your existence. This has the potential to spawn a <i>qashmal</i>who is to you as you were to the mortal who donated hir body to you. (In effect, \u201creturning to the source\u201d.)<br /> <br /> Going to a River of Death, and <i>not</i> returning; instead, moving directly on to whatever afterlives are available to humanity. <br /> <br /> Turning yourself over to the God-Machine, which uses an Occult Matrix to purge you of the Divine Fire and to substitute its own mechanisms within you, effectively converting you into an Angel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-22-2016, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:39:36-07:00","id":955685,"title":"","content":"I've never gotten the instability argument. Vampires are unstable. Mages are unstable. Wetewolves are unstable as fuck. Mummies? They're themed around age and stagnation, and yet they're still super unstable. Humans are unstable. You can learn to live with instability. Drifter's Path of the Quenched is still a change. It's going from being unstable to being less unstable- which is also what becoming human is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T14:07:20-07:00","id":955878,"title":"","content":"Roles to achieve the Elemental and Beast paths? Honestly, no idea, I haven't actually read the 2e release from cover to cover yet, so I'm I'm still kind of in the dark about the way the new Pilgrimages work. That said, off the top of my head...<br /> <br /> Elemental: Prometheans on this path would most be drawn to Cuprum, which revolves around refining the spirit by attaining oneness with the world around them. Secondary Refinements would include Ferrum, for physically honing the body and understanding how it melds with the world around it, and Mercurius, to understand the way that Pyros refines itself into the life energies of nature. Argentum (Spirits) is an optional pursuit for those who want to become spirits as well.<br /> <br /> Beast: I can see this as a combination of Cuprum (spiritual refinement) and a new Aurum role; the Promethean still wants to become a living, flesh-and-blood creature, it just wants to become an animal rather than a human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}